    id: 'approval',
    tab: 'Human approval',
    title: 'Pause for a person, for as long as it takes',
    intro:
      'This transfer waits for manual approval on large amounts, then moves the money. Retries, state persistence, and failure handling are the engine’s job, so none of them appear here.',
    points: [
      ['waitUntil hibernates.', 'The workflow can pause for a day or longer, consuming zero resources, then resume exactly where it left off.'],
      ['Signals wake it up.', 'approve(...) is called from the outside world: an API handler, a queue consumer, or a human.'],
      ['Automatic checkpoints.', 'Completed actions are persisted, so a resumed workflow never repeats work it has already done.'],
    ],
    java: approvalJava,
    kotlin: approvalKotlin,
  },
  {
    id: 'saga',
    tab: 'Saga',
    title: 'Undo the steps that already happened',
    intro:
      'An order touches three systems that share no transaction. When shipping fails, the charge and the reservation have to be reversed, in the right order, even if the process dies halfway through.',
    points: [
      ['Pair each step with its undo.', 'A @Compensate method sits next to the @Execute it reverses.'],
      ['Skipper unwinds in reverse order.', 'When the workflow fails, every completed step is compensated, last one first.'],
      ['The happy path stays readable.', 'The workflow method lists the steps and nothing else.'],
    ],
    java: sagaJava,
    kotlin: sagaKotlin,
  },
  {
    id: 'agent',
    tab: 'AI agent',
    title: 'An agent loop that survives a restart',
    intro:
      'An agent asks a model what to do next, runs the tool it picked, and repeats. Written as a workflow, every turn is saved, so a crash on turn nine resumes on turn nine.',
    points: [
      ['Model calls are checkpointed.', 'A finished inference is never paid for twice, and the agent never acts on a second, different answer.'],
      ['Tools run once.', 'A tool call that sent an email or moved money is not repeated when the agent resumes.'],
      ['Outages are retried.', 'Rate limits and timeouts back off on the retry strategy you choose.'],
    ],
    java: agentJava,
    kotlin: agentKotlin,
  },
  {
    id: 'team',
    tab: 'Agent team',
    title: 'Fan out to specialists, then join',
    intro:
      'Three specialist agents review an insurance claim in parallel, each as its own child workflow, and an adjudicator reconciles what they found. The same shape fits any fan-out, with or without models.',
    points: [
      ['Children are durable too.', 'Each specialist retries and resumes independently of the others and of its parent.'],
      ['Join on your own terms.', 'Wait for every answer, or set a deadline and carry on with the ones that arrived.'],
      ['Orchestration is plain code.', 'Who runs, in what order, and what happens on disagreement is not left to a model.'],
    ],
    java: teamJava,
    kotlin: teamKotlin,
  },
  {
    id: 'timers',
    tab: 'Timers',
    title: 'Processes that take weeks',
    intro:
      'Sending an invoice, chasing it three times, and escalating is one method that runs for three weeks. No cron job, no status column, and no table of reminders due.',
    points: [
      ['Durable timers.', 'A wait of a week costs nothing while it runs and survives every deploy in between.'],
      ['Wake early on an event.', 'The same wait ends the moment the payment signal arrives.'],
      ['The loop is the schedule.', 'What happens next is the next line, not a row in a jobs table.'],
    ],
    java: timerJava,
    kotlin: timerKotlin,
  },
